# target: boot/pi2/config.txt
# mode: write
# checker: scripts/line_ending_check.py
# why: Also decidable, and gated because the failure LOOKS like success. `.gitattributes` declares
# why: `boot/**` as `eol=lf` since U-Boot reads a trailing CR as part of every FILENAME: every entry
# why: fails while the menu renders perfectly, because a trailing CR in a display string just returns
# why: the cursor. Two card reflashes and two wrong theories (backlog/26).
# why:
# why: The plant must DIFFER from what is on disk - writing the same bytes back changes nothing, which
# why: is how the first draft got blessed to "no finding".
# why:
# why: The carriage returns are DECLARED as `\u000d`, not written literally. Spelled literally they
# why: would be the case FILE's own line endings, and `* text=auto` made those CRLF on a Windows
# why: checkout and LF everywhere else - so the fixture would measure the checkout rather than the
# why: checker, passing here and finding nothing on Linux CI. `.gitattributes` now pins `*.case` to
# why: `eol=lf` as well; both halves are needed, because an editor can still hand back CRLF.
--- plant ---
# A probe config planted by a conformance case.\u000d
kernel=kernel7.img\u000d
arm_64bit=0\u000d
enable_uart=1\u000d
--- expect ---
error[GS0102]: a tracked text file carries CRLF line endings
    |
    = rule: backlog/26
    = why: A CRLF in a boot config boots NOTHING while showing a perfect menu: U-Boot reads
           the trailing CR as part of every filename. It cost two reflashes before it was
           gated.
    = help: `conform` fixes this by rewriting the file with LF endings.
    = note: `py scripts/conform.py --explain GS0102` for the long form

  line_ending_check.py reported:
  | CARRIAGE RETURNS in files that must be LF:
  | (7 more lines of explanation, which the frame above covers - `py scripts/line_ending_check.py` for all of it)
